{"t": 1794123629.361401, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Flagging a production reconciliation regression introduced by this change (commit 8c2f1d0): [Sentry LEDGER-WORKER-9A](https://sentry.io/organizations/acme/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/). First seen in ledger-worker@2026.11.3; Sentry reports expected 1100 minor units, got 1099. The commit replaces `round(amount_minor * rate)` with `int(amount_minor * rate)` in worker/rates.py, truncating rather than rounding to the nearest minor unit.\n\nThe local fix restores the exact pre-change expression: `return round(amount_minor * rate)`. Seven direct regression cases passed, covering rounding up/down, negative amounts, zero, ties-to-even, and exact conversion. Illustrative reproduction (not event inputs): convert(1000, 1.0999) returned 1099 before and now returns 1100. `python -m pytest -q` found no tests in the supplied checkout (exit 5).", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
